[38;5;252m[1m## What the C actually does[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The library is two functions, and the interesting part is a type mismatch across translation units. [38;5;10minclude/match.h[0m has [38;5;10mtypedef double float_t[0m, but [38;5;10msrc/spectral_contrast.c[0m includes only [38;5;10m<math.h>[0m — so [3mits[23m [38;5;10mfloat_t[0m is C99's [38;5;10mfloat_t[0m, which is [38;5;10mfloat[0m on x86-64 glibc. [38;5;10mmatch[0m therefore hands [38;5;10mdouble[0m VLAs to a function that walks them as [38;5;10mfloat[0m. I confirmed this in the disassembly ([38;5;10mmovss[0m/[38;5;10mmulss[0m, 4-byte stride in [38;5;10mspectral_contrast[0m; [38;5;10mmovsd[0m, 8-byte stride in [38;5;10mmatch[0m), not just from the headers. The existing translation already modelled this correctly.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Bugs found and fixed in the Rust[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Three SSE [1mdestination-operand roles[22m were inverted relative to GCC's [38;5;10m-O0[0m codegen. GCC makes the freshly loaded value the two-address destination and the accumulator the source; the Rust [38;5;10mfp.rs[0m helpers were called with the opposite roles (and the module docs asserted the opposite of what GCC does). This is observable: with NaN operands, SSE returns the [3mdestination[23m NaN quieted, so [38;5;10mspectral_contrast[0m's returned [38;5;10mdouble[0m had a different NaN payload. Fixed in [38;5;10mtotal[0m, [38;5;10msmoothen[0m and [38;5;10mdot_product[0m. A mutation check confirms reverting either [38;5;10mdot_product[0m fix makes the suite fail.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Also fixed a manifest error ([38;5;10mcargo[0m rejects hyphens in library target names) and deleted [38;5;10msrc/matcher.rs[0m, a stale orphan duplicate of [38;5;10mmatch.rs[0m that referenced non-existent items and was not in the module tree.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Correction to a documented assumption[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m initially recorded [38;5;10mmatch(…, bins=0, …)[0m as a benign out-of-bounds write. It is not: the zero-length VLA's base [3mis[23m [38;5;10mmatch[0m's own [38;5;10m%rsp[0m, so [38;5;10mdifferentiate[0m's [38;5;10mv[length-1][0m store zeroes the return address [38;5;10mcall preprocess[0m pushed at [38;5;10m%rsp-8[0m, and the C reliably segfaults. I found this by segfaulting my own test binary, then confirmed it in a forked child. [38;5;10mtests/ub.rs[0m now measures the crash rather than assuming behaviour, with a control test proving the probe can distinguish crashing from clean exit.[0m[0m
